 "text": "9/29/26, 9:39 AM\nFeatures\n\nThis function enables you to adjust the screen layout to best suit your requirements. The fields visible on the screen have been\ngrouped into units that you can distribute among the individual tabs.\n\nActivities\nYou have the following options:\n\ne If you want to use the standard SAP layout, do not make any changes.\ne If you want to define your own layout then establish the following settings:\n\no a.ln Customizing, choose |)+Move-In/Out } Move-In + Configure Tabs for Move-In Screen \u00a7. Here you can define\n\nyour own layout.\n\no b.Enter the layout in Customizing as a default layout in Customizing under |)*SAP Utilities > Basic\nSettings/Enterprise Structure \u00bb Define Default Layout for Tabs\n\nService Notifications and Orders\n\nUse\n\nIn Customizing under |}*Device Management > Meter Reading \u00bb Basic Settings \u00bb Define Control Parameters fir Meter Reading\nData Processing, \u00bb you can configure the system to create a service order or service notification for the move-in meter reading\n(provided that plausible meter readings do not already exist for the metering devices). You can establish this settings separately\nfor each division.Customizing entries with an empty company code key are relevant to this process, since the system does not yet\nknow the company code in move-in initial processing. You can use enhancement ECSBTMRI]I (Assign default values for creation of\n\nservice notifications/orders).\n\nYou can also do this in Customizing under |}\u2018Device Management \u00bb Meter Reading \u00bb Basic Settings \u00bb Define Control Group for\nCreation of Multiple MR Orders 3) ., you define whether the system creates service notifications or service orders, and whether\nthese or stored at device, device location or connection object level.\n\nAlternatively, you can integrate the creation of service notifications and orders into a workflow, in which case creation is not\nimmediate but postponed. You do this in Customizing under Define System Parameters for Move-In and Move-Out . Prerequisites\nfor this are the method MovelnDocument.MeterReadingServicelnitiate (Trigger service management for meter reading) and the\nparameter DelayedMeterReadServ V in event MovelnDocument.Created for object type MOVEINDOC (move-in document).\n\nIf you reverse a move-in, the system adjusts the status of the service notifications/orders generated during move-in creation as\n\nfollows:\n\ne The status Completed is allocated to the service notifications.\ne The status Not executed is allocated to service orders that were not released.\n\ne The status Technically completed is allocated to service orders that were released.\n\nIf you change a move-in date, the system proceeds as though the move-in had been reversed and re-created for another date.\n",
